{
  "name": "engine-restarts",
  "description": "Issue 86: a session survives many engine starts. The sandbox attenuates each read-only grant from a fixed table it never returns a slot of (openkal 0.20.0, Windows and Linux alike), and 0.21.0 spent nine grants a start on Windows and eleven on Linux; this fixture restarts the engine eight times over and after each expects an answer again. With 0.22.0's narrower, merged grant set a start spends two or three slots and the loop passes. macOS keeps its conventional roots for now (the plan's §3.4 owns its table), so the fixture does not run there.",
